depgraph: skip _select_atoms_probe for atoms that dep_check() cannot drop

Sub-series: A (probe, match and config memos) - patch 10 of 10; applies to 3.0.83 with only the earlier patches of this sub-series.
Of these it needs 0001, 0002, 0004, 0005, 0012, 0013, 0014 only.
In the 25-patch ladder this was patch 0022; the step figures below were measured there, on top of 0001-0021 of that order.
Ported to upstream 73646c35d: unchanged (line numbers only)

_slot_operator_update_probe runs _select_atoms_probe(), i.e. dep_check()
over all dependency strings of a replacement parent, only to ask whether
one atom is among the selected atoms. An atom that stands at the top level
of a dependency list (outside every "||" group), is a plain Atom, is not
for a virtual/ package and is not in package.provided cannot be dropped by
dep_check(). _select_atoms_probe_certain() returns the set of those atoms
from use_reduce() alone (kept per root, package and USE for all
backtracking runs), and the probe is run only when the atom is not in that
set. The set is empty wherever the argument does not hold: before the
graph is complete, with --ignore-built-slot-operator-deps, without
local_config, during virtual expansion, for an invalid dependency string,
and after a config warning was printed (_probe_bounds_allowed of patch
0014).

On top of patches 0001-0021, resolve seconds before -> after
(median of the runs, at least 2 per figure):
  start 24.0 -> 23.0, holds 12.2 -> 11.8, masks 25.4 -> 24.1,
  py313 15.1 -> 14.4, bdeps 17.5 -> 16.9, policykit 12.4 -> 12.0
  sum of six 106.6 -> 102.2 (-4.4 s, -1.0 % of the stock sum 447.5)
Patches 0001-0022 together: 447.5 -> 102.2 s (-77 %); 447.5 is the
stock sum of the ladder run of 2026-11-20, stock was not run again here.

Kept as its own patch although the step is just under 5 s: a distinct
mechanism with its own correctness argument, and its step was between 4.4
and 5.9 s in all three orders that were measured.

Weak spots and what was not checked:
* Depends on dep_check() internals (what _expand_new_virtuals,
  dep_wordreduce and dep_zapdeps do with a top-level atom); a change there
  must revisit it. The probe may now run later than before or not at all,
  which is safe only inside one _slot_operator_trigger_reinstalls loop (the
  premise of patch 0001).

Origin: written by AI agents (Claude) in the emerge-fast job, 2026-11-17..20;
isolated from the full patch and measured on 2026-11-20..21. Not a human-written
change. Base: Portage 3.0.83. Test: `emerge -p -uND @world` on six states of
one system image, one resolve at a time; every run gave the same merge list
in the same order, the same number of backtracking attempts and the same
package count as unpatched 3.0.83.
